  "notes": "Read in a real browser from the official Public Notice of the 2026 General Election (Auditor Krystal Lloyd, dated Oct 14, 2026), linked from the www.webstercountyia.gov homepage; the bare webstercountyia.gov host returns Cloudflare error 526. No sample ballots are posted. Supervisor District 1 is on Fort Dodge 10, Fort Dodge 11, Badger/Cooper/Newark and Colfax/Hardin/Washington/Webster/Yell; District 4 on Fort Dodge 1, 2, 3 and 6. The notice does not print vote-for counts, so seats are null for Soil & Water (3 candidates) and Ag Extension (1 candidate); township offices assumed vote-for-one. Township offices listed as 'No Candidate' are recorded with empty candidate arrays (Badger trustee and clerk, Deer Creek clerk, Hardin, Lost Grove and Otho trustees, Johnson trustee vacancy). Notice lists no hospital trustee race and no county, city or school public measures (only Constitutional Amendment 1). Names copied as printed with stray PDF spacing removed (e.g., 'Jeff rey' -> Jeffrey, 'Dav e' -> Dave, 'T homas' -> Thomas)."
}